From a6d8c8940539dc62809102228f0d096b9d422220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:29:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 39/41] Safarium: content-setting icons in the address field,
 native popover
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The location bar hook UpdateContentSettingsIcons() now reaches the tab bar.
The current page's indicators come from Chrome's ContentSettingImageModel
(pop-ups blocked, location / notifications / camera / microphone in use or
blocked, automatic downloads, sound muted…) and sit in the address field,
right to left from the page menu, after the tab alert; up to three, SF
Symbols where one fits and Chrome's icon otherwise. Clicking one shows
Chrome's ContentSettingBubbleModel as a native NSPopover under it: title,
message, blocked items as links, the allow / block choice, Manage, Done.
The choice is committed when the popover closes, as Chrome's bubble does;
it closes when the tab changes.

The hover reload button now appears left of the indicators, so they (and a
popover anchored to one) never move when the pointer enters the field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
